flowchart TB
    accTitle: What the demo sets up
    accDescr: You run bash demo/seed.sh. It generates the secret key of Paperless and the passwords of the demo into demo/.env, and starts Paperless-ngx with Redis and Nextcloud with its background jobs in Docker, on 127.0.0.1 alone. Paperless reads five synthetic letters. Paperless Sync, a pinned signed release, writes each one into the files of the archive account paperless, which shares the archive read-only with jamie. occ paperless_unified_search:setup connects the app to Paperless, with the API token through a pipe. A search as jamie for invoice shows three Paperless documents, and the script prints the addresses and the accounts to sign in with.

    run(["bash demo/seed.sh"])
    secrets["demo/.env: the secret key<br>and the passwords, generated"]
    start["`Docker: **Paperless-ngx** with Redis,<br>**Nextcloud** with its background jobs`"]
    letters["Paperless reads five<br>synthetic letters"]
    sync["`**Paperless Sync** writes them<br>into the files of the<br>archive account paperless`"]
    share["paperless shares the archive<br>read-only with jamie"]
    setup["`occ **paperless_unified_search:setup**,<br>the token through a pipe`"]
    found(["jamie searches for invoice:<br>three Paperless documents"])

    run --> secrets --> start --> letters --> sync --> share --> setup --> found

    classDef person fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
    classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
    classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
    class run person
    class secrets,start,letters,sync,share,setup bot
    class found done
